  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 357 AM EDT Tue Jul 7 2026\n\nUpper level flow remains mostly zonal through the period, with \noccasional weak subtropical shortwaves moving across the southern \nCONUS. The sfc boundary left behind the remnants of Arthur will \ncontinue to drape across the area, acting as a guide for any system \nto latch onto. This results in daily low to moderate shower and \nthunderstorm chances. A few storms through the week may become \nstrong to severe dependent on diurnal destabilization. No widespread \nsevere is expected at this time.\n\nA slightly stronger shortwave on Monday may bring gustier \nconditions, even outside thunderstorms. Winds of 10 to 15 mph may \ngust out of the southwest to 20 to 25 mph.\n\nTemperatures to remain seasonable with the minimally amplitudinal \nflow. Highs in the mid 80s to low 90s can be expected.",
